cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OEV in your work, please cite it."
title: "OEV: a 184M-parameter neural decision engine"
authors:
  - given-names: Divyanshu
    family-names: Dhruv
    github: divyanshudhruv
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/divyanshudhruv/oev"
url: "https://github.com/divyanshudhruv/oev"
abstract: "OEV is a small neural decision engine. Instead of generating text, it scores typed answer options (choice, yes/no, ordinal score) directly: state, question and every option are packed into one sequence, and one forward pass returns a calibrated probability distribution. The single 184M model scores 0.7705 on typed-decisions above laya's 0.766 from 421M parameters, reaches 0.8594 on Banking77 from one soup checkpoint, transfers to zero-shot emotion at 0.8700 and to adversarial NLI at 0.5750, and answers a single question in 22.2 ms on a Tesla T4."
keywords:
  - decision-model
  - classification
  - calibration
  - system-one
  - deberta
